    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis explores the conflation of neurodiversity with low-income, underprepared students within higher education institutions, arguing that this mislabeling perpetuates pedagogical inertia and hinders educational pedagogical progress. By examining these elite systematic bureaucratization of neurodivergence and their labeling they inaccurately perpetuate these distinct separate groups being interchangeable. This research shows how this bureaucratization of neurodivergence and their labeling allow these institutions to absolve themselves from taking responsibility and changing their curriculum.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
